<p>➤ $15 USD via PayPal</p>
<p>➤ A signed, digital certificate of achievement </p>
<p>➤ 1-year CraftPix memberships for up to 5 team members (Worth ~$48 USD)<br></p>
<p><br></p>
<hr>
<h2>🎯 RATING:</h2>
<p>When submission is over, there will be a 48 hour rating period. These are the criteria:</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>➤ Enjoyment </strong>- how fun it was to play the game<strong><br><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>➤ Presentation </strong>- how well the visuals, sound, colors, etc, work together, and also controls/gameplay<strong><br><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>➤ Art &amp; Audio</strong> - graphics, sound, how well things are styled and look<strong><br><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>➤ Use of theme</strong> - how well the theme is integrated<strong><br><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>➤ Use of prerequisite </strong>- how well the prerequisite is integrate<strong><br></strong></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><em>▸After the voting period has ended, a Judge panel will assess a bracket of games to be chosen to receive a prize (See &quot;Prizes&quot; section above).</em><br></p>
<hr>
<h2>📜 RULES:</h2>
<h2></h2>
<p>➤ Keep the game content clean (no explicit, NSFW or disturbing graphics)<br><br></p>
<p>➤ Keep the game content in English (except for the title; it can be in any language)<br><br></p>
<p>➤You are allowed to change/submit a late entry 6 hours after the Jam ends, and you can do so through our Discord<br><br></p>
<p>➤ Game files cannot be edited after the submission deadline. The following six hours are only for new late submissions. To update an existing entry, you must delete it and resubmit it through the late-submission channel, which may reset its ratings.<br><br></p>
<p>➤ You can&#x27;t win 2 prizes in the same category (we won&#x27;t consider your lower ranking game for judging)<br><br></p>
<p>➤ To be eligible for prizes, you must be in our <a href="https://discord.gg/micro-jam-1190868995226730616" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin">Discord community</a>.<br></p>
<hr>
<details>
  <summary><h1>➤❓ FAQ:</h1></summary>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ If I&#x27;m in a team, do all members have to submit the game?<strong> </strong></summary>
    <p>No, only one person should submit it. You can add your team members to the game page.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Can I submit a game I already made?</summary>
    <p>No, you can only submit games made in the given timeframe. We don&#x27;t check, but just don&#x27;t~</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Can I use premade assets?</summary>
    <p>Yes, absolutely! If you have permission or if it&#x27;s your own, go for it!</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Can I use AI (artificial intelligence)?</summary>
    <p>Yep, you can! AI is a great tool that can help developers, and you should definitely try to take advantage of it.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ What&#x27;s a prerequisite?</summary>
    <p>A prerequisite is something that your game must follow. It is voted on and is released once the Jam starts.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Does my game have to follow the theme and prerequisite?</summary>
    <p>No, it doesn&#x27;t have to. But just remember that those are both a part of the rating criteria, so try to integrate them into your game.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Is there a prize for winning?</summary>
    <p>Yes, we offer numerous prizes! Check the &quot;Prizes&quot; section above.</p>
  </details>
  
  <details>
    <summary>➤ Can someone win 2 awards?</summary>
    <p>Yes and no. Someone can win both a top 3 award as well as a &quot;Best Ziva/GameMaker Entry&quot; Award. Their prize will be both of the awards, (E.G. obtaining a role in Discord and obtaining CraftPix key whilst getting 2 certificates) and the cash prize.</p>
  </details>
